# BASILISK — the sky serpent that spits fire (owner survey 2026-08-18: "flying
# snake-looking things that spam fireballs... the fire is the main problem").
# Clean-room: a long ribbon body, a shell-plated skull at the head, meat down
# the spine, blubber along the flanks so it hangs in the air the way every
# other creature here does.
#
# It is the reason fire exists as a system (v0.63.0): a whale rams, a kraken
# grabs, and a basilisk sets your gasbags alight from a distance you have to
# close. Its own head is armoured — you fight it from the side or the tail.
#
# Preview it without booting the game:
#
#   godot --headless --path . --script tools/ship_preview.gd -- ships/basilisk.ship
#
#   K  shell (the plated skull)   M  meat (spine)   W  blubber (flanks)
#
# Head to the RIGHT (Ship.visual_facing mirrors the drawing when it turns).
# Keep it ONE connected ribbon — a severed tail should fall away as its own
# piece, which the wall model already does for free.

origin 12 2

